{
  "request": {
    "model": "nomic-embed-text:latest",
    "input": [
      "Synthetic nurse note for software testing. No real patient data.\n\nThe nurse reviews a commercial driver's symptoms alongside information from a witness, the treating team and an older workplace form, because each source describes a different part of the story; the occupational record retains those differences and identifies completed current findings without turning a booking, a family account or a recollection into a measured patient result.\n\nThe current GP and medication review confirm established type 2 diabetes managed by diet and exercise alone, with no glucose-lowering medicine or insulin prescribed, and document that driving-relevant comorbidities have been assessed with no disqualifying effect; the driver mentions that an uncle uses injections, but those medicines belong to the uncle, and a previous referral proposing tablets was never implemented as a current treatment change.\n\nThe usual work involves coupling trailers, checking mirrors, interpreting radio messages and responding to pedestrians in a loading area, with breaks that can be delayed when deliveries run late; the driver explains which difficulty occurred while stationary and which was noticed during ordinary duties, rather than claiming that quiet conversation in the clinic reproduces every task in the cab.\n\nThe nurse reads the summary back to the driver to check the chronology and separates agreement about the wording from verification of a medical finding, then attaches the identified clinical material; any decision about further investigation or work allocation remains for the reviewing professional, and the note itself does not certify that all relevant clinical questions have been answered.\n"
    ],
    "truncate": false
  },
  "provider_called": true,
  "status": "completed",
